(7670711, 1251933, 31637, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i> Nit picky, but your horizon is tilted a tad. It''s still an 8 from me, but once someone pointed out tilted horizons, they stick out a lot when I view them. :)<br/> <br/>But this is one of the few that I feel actually has a foreground, middle, and far part to the photo. :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hmm...I see it now. I think I submitted the wrong file to the challenge, because I recall fixing the horizon distortion. Thanks for the 8!</td>', 'Originally posted by vawendy: Nit picky, but your horizon is tilted a tad. It''s still an 8 from me, but once someone pointed out tilted horizons, they stick out a lot when I view them. :) But this is one of the few that I feel actually has a foreground, middle, and far part to the photo. :)   Hmm...I see it now. I think I submitted the wrong file to the challenge, because I recall fixing the horizon distortion. Thanks for the 8!', '2020-07-24 01:24:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7670730, 1251810, 67145, '<td valign="top">I saw this a day or two ago and have been meaning to comment .. <br/>it literally takes my breath away .. <br/>I''m on my phone so I won''t write a novel lol .. <br/>but this is up there as one of THE most beautiful scenes I''ve ever seen .. <br/>of course my penchant for black and white helps .. and how much I absolutey love the mist/fog in a photo .. <br/>but even if they weren''t elements that really tug at me ..  this would still speak volumes to that place in us all that connects to the incredible beauty that can be found in nature .. <br/>many congrats on the blue .. so perfect for the challenge .. and what a great score .. and of course that it got on your profile page .. <br/>no mean feat in this day and age in dpc .. well for me at least .. probably not so much for you ..!!.. ;)<br/> <br/>appears I did write that novel .. lol ..</td>', 'I saw this a day or two ago and have been meaning to comment .. it literally takes my breath away .. I''m on my phone so I won''t write a novel lol .. but this is up there as one of THE most beautiful scenes I''ve ever seen .. of course my penchant for black and white helps .. and how much I absolutey love the mist/fog in a photo .. but even if they weren''t elements that really tug at me ..  this would still speak volumes to that place in us all that connects to the incredible beauty that can be found in nature .. many congrats on the blue .. so perfect for the challenge .. and what a great score .. and of course that it got on your profile page .. no mean feat in this day and age in dpc .. well for me at least .. probably not so much for you ..!!.. ;) appears I did write that novel .. lol ..', '2020-07-24 04:55:02.000000', NULL, 0),
